goal "prospective-dogfooding" { serves ["honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "Use real prospective task acceptance, scoped ownership, feature-boundary checks, independent reviews and canonical finish. Preserve historical development-agent play and new procedural provenance honestly. The game is a primary BlaBla dogfood: identify concrete workflow friction and deliver useful small tooling improvements without repeated per-edit gates or a parallel evidence ledger." expect ["contract::bootstrap"] state "active" }
goal "history-to-mars" { serves ["full-historical-arc"] statement "Deliver a connected earned zero-player journey from Stone Age settlements through industrial and planetary civilization to viable Mars colonization. Early and middle ages must offer meaningful autonomous alternatives, discoveries, rivalries and visible consequences in their own right, not merely launch prerequisites. Existing farming, towns, exchange, culture, government, industry and paid off-world mechanics do not by themselves establish rich whole-history coverage. Extend era-specific content through researched coherent procedural features, keeping unimplemented mechanics explicitly planned rather than promoting catalogue entries to delivered coverage. No free technology, artificial resource grants or calendar-only unlocks substitute for real progression. Keep each unavailable capability honestly planned until its implementation and causal evidence exist. The authoritative six-minute clock adds ten years, with a hundred-year milestone every ten ticks; routine event/review injections add no years. Explicit deliberate feature or Director-event advances may add history once with a visible cause and receipt, independent of baseline clock accounting. Ordinary turn count alone does not move history." expect ["campaign::five-civilizations", "campaign::bounded-era", "future-outcomes::colonies-need-spaceflight"] state "active" }
goal "interconnected-world" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies"] statement "Production, supply routes, research, population, culture and political agreements produce observable cross-system consequences." expect ["campaign::route-integrity", "campaign::nonnegative-population"] state "active" }
goal "six-clear-fast-agents" { serves ["fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "Five procedural civilizations and a procedural Director choose independent legal actions using seeded weighted finite-state behaviors with distinct soft preferences. Runtime play requires no LLM calls or developer presence. Preserve fair per-actor admission, exact commands, atomic upkeep, standing commitments and honest causal presentation. Explicit activation and real hosted or clearly labeled local evidence distinguish implemented controllers from genuinely running unattended service." expect ["concurrency::idle-civilization-does-not-block-peer", "strategy-actions::eligible-exact-action-survives-due-upkeep", "strategy-actions::refusal-commits-neither-upkeep-nor-action", "campaign::accepted-command-advances-once", "campaign::refused-command-preserves-revision"] state "active" }
goal "scientific-and-political-endings" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "full-historical-arc"] statement "The required full journey includes an earned viable Mars settlement with genuine supply and survival consequences. A functioning federation remains an alternative designed outcome with visible progress and counterplay. Deliver coherent stages without pretending missing space-age mechanics or a future date already provide colonization." expect ["future-outcomes::colonies-need-spaceflight", "future-outcomes::outcome-is-final"] state "active" }
goal "cultural-victory" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies"] statement "A later increment supports a voluntarily adopted cultural network rooted in attractive functioning cities, with contestable influence and meaningful counterplay." expect ["victories::cultural-network-is-an-ending"] state "active" }
goal "economic-victory" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies"] statement "A later increment supports sustained pivotal resilient trade across independent partners, with substitution and renegotiation counterplay." expect ["victories::resilient-trade-is-an-ending"] state "active" }
goal "military-victory" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies"] statement "A later increment supports supplied political hegemony with occupation, reconstruction and legitimacy costs, not merely territory counting." expect ["victories::supplied-hegemony-is-an-ending"] state "active" }
goal "watchable-spectator" { serves ["fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "The main reference is Civilization games and recognizable Civilization-like look and feel is a hard outcome: an original map-led world with legible terrain and water, inhabited cities, territorial borders, productive sites, actual routes, selected-faction progress and meaningful local events. Camera, playback and inspection are the only human controls; no faction orders or event triggers. Evaluate actual desktop and narrow pixels, hierarchy, comfort and comprehension, not source tests or decorative component counts alone." expect ["procedural-civilizations::spectator-never-commands-the-world", "spectator::cues-come-from-new-window"] state "active" }
goal "durable-faithful-replay" { serves ["honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "Versioned seeded commands reproduce committed outcomes and restart preserves world and controller state. Recordings distinguish procedural policies, historical development agents, contract probes and mixed history. A new policy version or explicit local observatory cannot silently reinterpret old inputs or overwrite the inhabited shared world." expect ["campaign::restart-preserves-world", "bootstrap::replay-identifies-its-source"] state "active" }
goal "public-updated-presentation" { serves ["honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "Each integrated feature is available at a public no-auth spectator link with an accurate change presentation; deployed version changes auto-reload without loops, preserving compatible observational preferences." expect ["spectator::reload-request-follows-version-policy"] state "active" }
goal "authoritative-live-world" { serves ["honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "Keep durable authoritative turns and protected authenticated command or procedural-service writes while public spectators remain read-only. Concurrent writes and repeated wakes commit only their accepted consequences once with controller memory and durable receipts. Preserve existing runs and history; a local observatory is not the shared world. Explicit activation and a verified supported wake source are required before claiming unattended hosting." expect ["concurrency::accepted-peer-action-commits-once", "procedural-civilizations::competing-wakes-do-not-double-act", "procedural-civilizations::duplicate-wake-preserves-world"] state "active" }

goal "development-moves-history" { serves ["full-historical-arc", "honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "Every calendar transition comes from either a durable six-minute clock tick adding ten years or a separately authorized deliberate feature/Director-event advance with a typed cause, stable identifier, visible reason and durable receipt. Intentional jumps never rebase or double-count clock intervals. Each ten clock ticks marks a hundred-year milestone. Ten-minute events and hourly review inject events without double-counting years; ordinary turns do not move calendar, and unimplemented future mechanics never block or silently unlock from time alone." expect ["campaign::turns-do-not-advance-calendar", "architecture::content-owns-feature-availability"] state "active" }

goal "ship-play-advance" { serves ["ship-play-advance", "honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "A working stage is shipped and actually played, then the Creative Director selects the next meaningful mechanic or historical milestone. Fun and balance are learned through live play; no indefinite polish or exhaustive campaign gate blocks roadmap progress." expect ["campaign::accepted-command-advances-once", "architecture::content-owns-feature-availability"] state "active" }
goal "dry-solid-data-driven" { serves ["dry", "solid", "data-driven"] statement "Enforce DRY, SOLID and DATA DRIVEN through falsifiable source boundaries, behavior scenarios proving shared rules and an independent semantic review. Shared catalogues feed legal choices and displays; the pure engine owns decisions; adapters and viewers cannot duplicate or override them. Structural GREEN is evidence for named facts, not proof of all three design principles." expect ["spectator-preview::renderer-uses-content", "spectator-preview::inspection-uses-the-same-content", "spectator-preview::viewer-delegates-rendering", "bootstrap::shared-command-schema", "architecture::content-owns-feature-availability", "architecture::command-effects-share-one-interpreter"] state "active" }

goal "tactical-and-strategic-systems" { serves ["tactics-and-strategy", "one-world-many-strategies"] statement "Immediate actions change concrete world facts while longer-lived programs, agreements and projects create slower strategic consequences across economic, scientific, political, cultural and military systems. The next trade increment demonstrates an immediate offer and a lasting consensual exchange with later shipments. Neither actions nor strategic state depend on rendering or the six-minute calendar." expect ["strategy::immediate-order-affects-persistent-commitment"] state "active" }
goal "spectator-comfort-and-history" { serves ["fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "Desktop and mobile viewing keep the map primary, offer touch-accessible inspection, simple English for non-native readers using familiar words, short direct sentences, no idioms or unnecessary jargon, consistent explained game terms, meaningful text emphasis on key facts and numbers, consistent semantic icons and color for resources, statistics, actions, status and outcomes, never color-only meaning, safe text rendering without injected HTML, tooltips with keyboard and tap-accessible equivalents, light/dark/system theme and adjustable effects. A clickable BlaBla footer sits beside version and a changelog with older releases collapsed. Live history has bounded cursor pages, stable inspection scroll and a new-events notice; virtualization is added only for genuinely large expanded views with accessible fallback." expect ["spectator::accessible-preferences", "hosting::bounded-history-pages"] state "active" delivery "required" applies-to ["system::spectator"] }
goal "fresh-world-version-boundaries" { serves ["ship-play-advance", "honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "Before release, new game versions may start fresh with explicit registered rules. Do not migrate existing worlds or reinterpret saved actions. Current-version restart preserves the same world; fresh initialization refuses an occupied hosted world. Historical read support is not an upgrade path, and no archive system is required to ship new mechanics." expect ["campaign::restart-preserves-world", "concurrency::invalid-action-preserves-world"] state "active" }
goal "measured-resource-budgets" { serves ["measured-resource-efficiency", "fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "Record reproducible finite workload baselines for simulation latency, observation/state/event bytes and counts, API page/query/row work, and mobile viewer frame/memory/visible-object behavior where the actual browser supports measurement. Assert deterministic count/payload limits and update affected budgets when a real feature changes them. Machine-specific elapsed times are evidence, not tight universal pass thresholds; unmeasured mobile or managed-host quotas remain explicitly unverified." expect ["performance::finite-workload-bounds", "performance::bounded-history-query", "performance::renderer-independent-work"] state "active" }
goal "deliberate-data-lifecycle" { serves ["measured-resource-efficiency", "honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "Keep one compact current state plus the bounded history and receipts needed for same-version integrity and replay. Use indexed pages and avoid repeated unchanged payloads or unnecessary duplicate state. Checkpoint writes remain atomic; ordinary retention must not discard required deduplication evidence. No world/save migrations before release, and no external stored data deletion is authorized." expect ["hosting::atomic-state-transition-receipt", "campaign::restart-preserves-world"] state "active" }
goal "growing-current-project-intent" { serves ["honest-incremental-delivery", "dry", "solid", "data-driven"] statement "As features grow, keep cohesive registered contracts, goals and system responsibilities current through scoped research, explicit affected-intent disposition and independent source review. A read-only registration inventory exposes forgotten .bla files without silently loading them. Coverage views distinguish explicit links from inference and do not turn prose or semantic guesses into proof." expect ["intent::changed-input-invalidates-disposition", "intent::unregistered-contract-is-visible"] state "active" }

goal "bounded-civilization-planning" { serves ["fast-agents-readable-spectacle", "tactics-and-strategy"] statement "Each civilization keeps at most two actionable plan items: a useful next action and one follow-up. Explicit queued, executing, blocked, failed and completed states retain a concrete result or reason. Execute the next useful action and reevaluate after a result, invalidation or blockage; do not stall on whole-game planning. This civilization planning bound is separate from the development team twelve-hour feature roadmap. No built-in planner may be mislabeled as a model agent." expect ["concurrency::actionable-plan-is-bounded", "concurrency::invalid-action-preserves-world"] state "active" }

goal "prepared-research-and-building-pool" { serves ["ship-play-advance", "one-world-many-strategies", "full-historical-arc"] statement "Each playable stage offers useful present research and building decisions and keeps a connected prepared successor pool ahead of live needs. Completed discoveries must lead to new meaningful productive or institutional commitments as features ship. Water management and Kiln firing require implemented shared input/output operation, pause controls and blocked-production evidence under an explicitly selected fresh registered configuration. Implemented local source does not by itself enable live choices. The two-item civilization plan limit does not cap the catalogue or the twelve-hour development queue." expect ["contract::manufacturing", "production::operating-inputs-are-atomic", "production::paused-building-preserves-inputs"] state "active" delivery "required" applies-to ["system::simulation"] }

goal "useful-conserved-frontiers" { serves ["ship-play-advance", "one-world-many-strategies", "data-driven"] statement "Founding transfers people from an explicitly selected owned source while preserving a viable source population, atomically paying costs and creating a useful location choice through one data-defined terrain-output catalogue. Fresh configuration establishes map identity; refused or contested actions spend nothing." expect ["frontiers::founding-conserves-population", "frontiers::source-remains-inhabited", "frontiers::refusal-spends-nothing"] state "active" }

goal "recoverable-local-disruption" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "tactics-and-strategy", "fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "Released disruption changes concrete local productive conditions and provides an affordable explicit recovery action. A civilization repairs its exact owned damaged city using canonical shared inputs; other settlements, people and buildings remain intact. Refused actions spend nothing. Spectators see current damage and the actual repair delta, while later production shows the consequence. Bounded component checks do not claim every disaster is released or that live recovery has occurred." expect ["recovery::exact-local-damage-reduction", "recovery::refused-repair-has-no-effects", "recovery::repair-preserves-people-and-buildings"] state "active" }

goal "consensual-public-projects" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "tactics-and-strategy"] statement "Civic institutions let independent partners promise and deliver a concrete shared public good. An exact agreed route binds immutable terms; recipient consent creates a delayed commitment, either partner may cancel, and due completion pays both complete contributions atomically or visibly fails without partial payment. Public repairs do not manufacture shipment history or a federation victory." expect ["public-projects::consent-creates-no-immediate-payment", "public-projects::consent-creates-no-immediate-repair", "public-projects::completion-needs-due-commitment", "public-projects::due-contributions-are-both-complete-or-neither", "public-projects::unfulfilled-project-spends-nothing", "public-projects::project-resolution-preserves-shipment-history"] state "active" }

goal "exact-consenting-trade-towns" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "A delivered compatible trade expansion lets the proposer name its exact source town and the partner's exact destination town. Recipient consent keeps those identities and immutable exchange terms; missing, foreign or changed endpoints refuse without substituting another town or spending stock. Earlier releases retain their recorded first-city behavior. Agents receive compact canonical site facts for the decision, and spectators inspect the same towns. This increment keeps civilization-wide stocks and existing delivery cadence; it does not claim terrain paths, distance costs or Navigation." expect ["trade-endpoints::proposal-binds-exact-owned-towns", "trade-endpoints::consent-preserves-promised-town-identities", "trade-endpoints::invalid-endpoint-consent-spends-nothing", "trade-endpoints::older-release-keeps-first-city-replay"] state "active" }

goal "lossless-compact-observations" { serves ["fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "An explicit compact observation view factors repeated canonical town and recipe facts while preserving every exact ordered legal action, existing plan semantics and immutable consent. Default clients remain compatible. Measure finite payloads honestly; no silent option truncation or universal speed claim." expect ["agent-observations::compact-view-preserves-every-exact-action", "agent-observations::compact-facts-resolve-canonical-identities", "agent-observations::stored-consent-keeps-its-original-terms", "agent-observations::formatting-never-mutates-the-world", "agent-observations::default-observation-remains-compatible"] state "active" }
goal "reconcile-uncertain-action-receipts" { serves ["fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "An already enrolled caller can read only its own accepted action key and original committed revision through a bounded read-only lookup. Missing receipts remain uncertainty, never a denial diagnosis or permission to retry. Private identities and command inputs are not disclosed; no read advances the world or expands access." expect ["action-receipts::receipt-read-has-no-world-effects", "action-receipts::receipt-read-keeps-owner-boundary", "action-receipts::receipt-read-never-exposes-private-input", "action-receipts::accepted-receipt-retains-committed-revision", "action-receipts::missing-receipt-is-not-a-denial-verdict"] state "active" }

goal "geographic-consensual-transport" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "tactics-and-strategy", "data-driven"] statement "New released land exchanges quote one deterministic passable path between exactly consenting towns. Shared path length determines an immutable acceptance-relative cadence; no cargo moves before a due successful exchange. Invalidated paths visibly block without rerouting or payment. Earlier abstract offers and agreements preserve their original terms and timing. This delivers periodic land logistics; Navigation still requires genuinely newly reachable transport." expect ["land-transport::new-geographic-quote-has-exact-shortest-path", "land-transport::eligible-geographic-consent-succeeds", "land-transport::funded-valid-due-exchange-delivers", "land-transport::geographic-delivery-waits-the-accepted-interval", "land-transport::consented-terms-and-schedule-survive-restart"] state "active" }
goal "operating-supply-through-consent" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "tactics-and-strategy", "data-driven"] statement "An authorized applied expansion lets partners choose a standing energy-for-materials exchange through the same exact-town consent, immutable quotes and due delivery rules. Both sides fund their complete cargo and upkeep before any transfer; imported fuel may support a later operating beat but cannot retroactively fund the earlier opening-stock allocation. Earlier food agreements and all exact legal choices remain intact. Local legal journeys and synthetic scarcity witnesses remain separately identified until genuine live play occurs." expect ["operating-resource-exchange::funded-due-fuel-exchange-delivers", "operating-resource-exchange::fuel-exchange-pays-gross-cargo-and-upkeep", "operating-resource-exchange::imported-fuel-does-not-fund-earlier-operation", "operating-resource-exchange::new-fuel-recipe-preserves-existing-consent"] state "active" }

goal "bounded-complete-choice-pages" { serves ["fast-agents-readable-spectacle", "measured-resource-efficiency"] statement "An optional compact paged observation exposes every exact action in canonical order through count-bounded pages, with shared facts on the first page and immutable consent retained. Cursors bind the run scope, revision, seat, exact observation time and projected view; stale continuations refuse explicitly without returning a different menu. Malformed selectors refuse before world access. Existing unpaged clients and mutation authority remain unchanged. Measure first-page savings and complete-traversal overhead separately; slicing a full projection is not a generation-speed claim." expect ["choice-pages::every-exact-choice-remains-reachable", "choice-pages::page-zero-facts-and-consent-remain-exact", "choice-pages::page-count-is-bounded-without-dropping-options", "choice-pages::stale-view-never-silently-restarts", "choice-pages::eligible-continuation-retains-observation-time", "choice-pages::malformed-cursor-refuses-before-world-access", "choice-pages::action-identity-binds-the-exact-intention", "choice-pages::existing-unpaged-formats-remain-compatible"] state "active" }

goal "faithful-recorded-route-map" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "fast-agents-readable-spectacle", "measured-resource-efficiency"] statement "The spectator map follows every retained land-path turn through one shared bounded projection. Older abstract links remain clearly schematic; invalid quotes never become invented shortcuts. Inspection preserves accepted cadence, exact towns and distinct current blockage versus historical delivery facts. Map detail limits never remove access to full route identity and ordered tiles. No moving cargo or travel estimate is inferred between actual exchange beats." expect ["route-map::eligible-recorded-path-keeps-every-turn", "route-map::older-links-remain-explicitly-schematic", "route-map::invalid-quotes-never-invent-a-shortcut", "route-map::projection-keeps-terms-history-and-world", "route-map::both-renderers-use-the-same-recorded-vertices", "route-map::bounded-map-detail-retains-complete-inspection"] state "active" }

goal "conserved-local-resident-support" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies"] statement "A gated shared resident-capacity rule makes conserved frontier founding affect the next local paid operations. Opening residents and complete resource vectors allocate atomically; paused or blocked recipes reserve neither. Current factored capacity and historical allocation receipts remain distinct, old releases preserve their output, and new rules are selected at fresh genesis." expect ["resident-capacity::funded-and-supported-recipe-operates", "resident-capacity::resources-and-residents-allocate-together", "resident-capacity::capacity-is-local-and-opening-only", "resident-capacity::founding-conserves-people-and-changes-later-support", "resident-capacity::old-releases-retain-resource-only-production"] state "active" }

goal "legible-civilization-decisions" { serves ["fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "A spectator can see what each civilization chose, its recorded reason when present, what actually changed and which next capabilities became reachable. An inspectable connected research/building tree distinguishes completed, available, locked and planned content from shared prerequisites and the applied release. Show exact important values and tap/keyboard explanations in simple English; never invent model reasoning or present a forecast as a recorded result." expect ["spectator-decisions::status-follows-canonical-availability", "spectator-decisions::reasons-and-deltas-have-recorded-evidence"] state "active" delivery "required" applies-to ["system::spectator", "system::simulation", "system::authoritative-host"] }


goal "visible-growing-world" { serves ["fast-agents-readable-spectacle", "honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "Deliver a substantial, coherent inhabited-landscape transformation that makes actual settlement population, constructed fields/workshops, terrain, water and territorial identity visibly distinct at normal play scale. Art Director owns a matched-camera desktop and narrow before/after comparison from committed world facts; Creative Director checks the connection to current play. Current outcome is partial: isolated buildings, route/layout fixes and small panels do not establish this visible milestone. Keep this outcome and a concrete next Art task visible until real pixels establish delivery; unavailable WebGL or physical-device evidence remains explicit. Source tests, task closure and added geometry counts cannot by themselves satisfy this goal; the linked rules cover only data fidelity, while visual delivery requires the separate actual outcome review." expect ["spectator-preview::renderer-uses-content", "route-map::projection-keeps-terms-history-and-world"] state "active" delivery "required" applies-to ["system::spectator"] }

goal "recurring-civilization-decisions" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "tactics-and-strategy", "ship-play-advance"] statement "Every procedural civilization maintains actual research, civic and exact-town construction commitments when legal choices exist. Seeded controllers choose, progress, complete and choose again without a developer returning to play. Weights and state machines may differ while required lanes avoid starvation; active work is not silently replaced. Blocked choices retain engine-derived reasons, idle actors do not stall peers or economy, and paid work survives recovery without double payment. Local, hosted and historical model evidence remain separate; actual choose-progress-complete-next-choice behavior is required." expect ["required-decisions::completion-exposes-next-required-choice", "required-decisions::hold-cannot-hide-actionable-obligations", "required-decisions::construction-pays-and-completes-once", "required-decisions::absent-actor-does-not-stop-world"] state "active" delivery "required" applies-to ["system::simulation", "system::agents", "system::authoritative-host"] }

goal "coastal-founding-expands-reach" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "full-historical-arc", "ship-play-advance"] statement "Navigation and a completed coastal Boat yard let an procedural civilization found an exact new coastal town beyond ordinary owned-frontier access, transferring existing residents and paying the same founding cost once. Deterministic ocean paths, explicit source/site facts and retained receipts make the new reach inspectable. Preserve paid land founding; actual applied founding and visible result remain pending until observed." expect ["contract::coastal-founding"] state "active" delivery "required" }


goal "connected-history-through-mars-catalogue" { serves ["full-historical-arc", "one-world-many-strategies", "ship-play-advance"] statement "Maintain coherent researched early, middle and late historical possibilities through useful procedural rules and connected current content. Runtime definitions name actual prerequisites, costs, effects and consumers. Keep unimplemented mechanics explicitly planned. Do not publish unused catalogue expansions, reference dumps or internal evidence merely to fill a roadmap; concise project direction and meaningful playable content take priority." expect ["contract::future-outcomes", "production::operating-inputs-are-atomic"] state "active" delivery "required" }

goal "productive-visible-research" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "tactics-and-strategy", "fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "An active research project advances from actual science produced each strategic beat rather than instantly draining a long idle bank. Use fresh registered rules and preserve current-version discoveries, reserves, progress and replay. Honest progress and remaining work are visible, and sufficiently productive civilizations may still finish cheap research in one beat. Observe an actual recorded civilization choice, intermediate progress where the production/cost warrants it, completion and next choice; never pad duration merely to conceal an empty content pool." expect ["contract::research-investment"] state "active" delivery "required" }

goal "inhabited-empire-map" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "tactics-and-strategy", "fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "Civilizations visibly grow beyond the five starter capitals into useful distinct towns, exact territorial production and learning sites, worked resources and strategically consequential unique wonders. Generate the selected map extent at genesis and preserve paid ownership and current-world history. Connect completed research and civic choices to new productive or institutional commitments, including actual effects on exact-town work. Actual recorded civilization settlement and site choices, resulting resource or research consequences and readable map evidence are required. A completed future catalogue is design delivery only; a zoom change, status panel or decorative marker alone cannot satisfy this outcome." expect ["contract::manufacturing", "contract::frontiers", "contract::coastal-founding", "contract::district-learning", "contract::worked-land", "contract::metal-learning", "contract::future-outcomes"] state "active" delivery "required" }

goal "autonomous-weighted-civilizations" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "fast-agents-readable-spectacle", "honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "A reproducible running observatory gives five civilizations distinct weighted finite-state behavior and a procedural Director without runtime LLM calls. Existing legal simulation mechanics determine all consequences. Controllers persist across restart, duplicate wakes do not double-act, and held commitments progress to new useful decisions. Show actual behavior on a Civilization-like observer map. A local-only running world is explicitly labeled and separate from the archived shared world; genuinely unattended hosted delivery requires verified supported scheduling." expect ["contract::procedural-civilizations"] state "active" delivery "required" applies-to ["system::procedural-controllers", "system::authoritative-host", "system::spectator"] }

goal "meaningful-food-security" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "tactics-and-strategy", "honest-incremental-delivery"] statement "Healthy starts can develop while geography, Food focus, staffed production, repairs and exact consenting transfers create meaningful household supply choices. Preserve current-version accounting and all paid Mars obligations. Actual required versus spent meals and recovery are inspectable. Conditional fixtures establish mechanics, not natural cooperation: retain the zero-natural-aid experiment and keep this outcome Partial until an ordinary fixed-seed campaign demonstrates useful autonomous resilience; never force healthy actors to donate or count an unnecessary gift as a rescue." expect ["contract::production", "contract::procedural-civilizations"] state "active" delivery "required" applies-to ["system::simulation", "system::procedural-controllers", "system::spectator"] }

goal "paid-institutional-cooperation" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "full-historical-arc", "fast-agents-readable-spectacle"] statement "Middle-history partners can explicitly consent to useful institutional teaching over actual trade. Two fresh paid institution-operation seasons over a live consenting corridor and complete teaching contributions produce bounded research work, not free technology or fake cargo. The observer distinguishes offers, consent, study, payment, work and separate discovery completion. Conditional current-mechanics fixtures do not prove naturally selected cooperation or balance; those outcomes remain open." expect ["contract::knowledge-compacts"] state "active" delivery "required" applies-to ["system::simulation", "system::procedural-controllers", "system::spectator"] }

goal "supplied-territorial-rivalry" { serves ["one-world-many-strategies", "full-historical-arc", "tactics-and-strategy"] statement "Early and middle civilizations can compare funded peaceful land with a finite supplied border incident over an exact unworked rival purchase. Real residents leave and return, consented existing commitments remain funded, one bounded clash can cause at most one accounted casualty, and current control has its own receipt. Observable conditional mechanics do not prove natural opportunity, pacing or strategic balance." expect ["contract::border-incidents"] state "active" delivery "required" applies-to ["system::simulation", "system::procedural-controllers", "system::spectator"] }
